# Project layout and workflow

Cargo workspace; crates live under `source/`. One pipeline stage per crate — never reach across stages (no typeck logic in codegen, no lexing in the parser, etc.).

| Crate | Owns |
|---|---|
| `source/phx-syntax` | Lexer, token stream, parser, AST (`ast/`), interner (`intern.rs`), source files/spans |
| `source/phx-compiler` | Resolver, typeck (incl. `ownership.rs`, `mono.rs`, intrinsic/std kernels), IR, lowering, codegen, modules, lints, linking, build orchestration |
| `source/phx-bytecode` | `PHX0` format: opcodes, instructions, sections, encode/decode, constant pool, **verifier** (`verify.rs`), stack-effect metadata |
| `source/phx-vm` | Interpreter, frames, VM errors, foreign/host functions |
| `source/phx-diagnostics` | Error types, codes, rendering, `explain` text — all user-facing diagnostics flow through here |
| `source/phx-cli` / `source/phx` | CLI commands, arg parsing, reporting / binary entry point |
| `std/` | Phoenix standard library written in Phoenix (`.phx`) |
| `website/` | Marketing site — **git submodule** → `phoenix-language/website` (separate repo, PRs, and deploy) |
| `tests/` | `integration/` (E2E + diagnostics fixtures), `cli/` (fixtures), `phx-test`, `ci/` (policy scripts) |

**Feature order** for any new language feature: lexer → parser → AST → resolver → typeck → IR → codegen → verifier → VM → std → tests. Don't skip the resolver for `#import`/multi-file work.

## Hard project policies

- **Stdlib-only**: no crates.io dependencies — CI (`just dep-check`) fails the build on any. Implement what you need in-tree.
- Edition 2024. Enforced lints: `missing_docs`, `missing_errors_doc`, `unwrap_used`, `expect_used`, `dbg_macro`, `print_stdout`, `print_stderr` are all **deny**; `clippy::pedantic` and `perf` warn (and `-D warnings` in CI makes warns fatal).
- Release profile is `panic = "abort"` — panics are never a recovery strategy.
- Diagnostics shown to Phoenix developers must include a span, a clear message, and a fix hint where possible. Never leak Rust panics, backtraces, or `Debug` dumps to them.

## Commands (Justfile)

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Build / test everything | `just build` / `just test` (`cargo test --workspace`) |
| Run a Phoenix file | `just run file.phx` or `just phx <args>` |
| Language E2E tests | `just test-lang` |
| Lint / format | `just lint` / `just fmt` |
| Full pre-commit gate | `just pre-commit` (fmt-check, clippy `-D warnings`, doc-check, dep-check, `cargo test --workspace`, test-lang) |
| Website local dev | `just website dev` (delegates to `website/justfile` submodule) |

Clone with `git clone --recurse-submodules`; existing clones run `git submodule update --init --recursive`. Website submodule workflow: see `.cursor/rules/website-submodule.mdc`.

## Completion gate

Before marking a task complete, suggesting a commit, or opening a PR:

1. Run `just pre-commit` from the repo root; fix and re-run until green.

Commit messages: `[stage]: description` — e.g. `[typeck]: enforce use-after-move diagnostics`, `[lower]: add IndexStore slice stores`. Each commit leaves the workspace building and passing tests. Never commit commented-out code or debug prints.
